#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:6
#: c7e3179b3f5244b3a0c458140bca8ea1
msgid "What is Harness Engineering?"
msgstr "什么是 Harness Engineering？"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:8
#: 40b04cc6a7f24754bc05de07f269e493
msgid ""
"*If Chapter 01 is the motivation and Chapter 05 is the method, this chapter "
"is the dictionary entry a skeptic should be able to read in fifteen "
"minutes.*"
msgstr "*如果说第 01 章是动机、第 05 章是方法，那么本章就是一位怀疑者应当能在十五分钟内读完的词条解释。*"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:11
#: d093b0574bf744329683f7acecb44fef
msgid ""
"Most readers will not arrive at this book linearly. Some will land here from"
" a search engine, a conference talk, or a colleague's Slack link. They need "
"one thing first: a **definition** — concise enough to cite, defended enough "
"to trust, and bordered enough to distinguish from the five disciplines the "
"field most often collapses into. This chapter delivers that definition in "
"five sections, followed by the Research Foundations and Hands-On tracks the "
"rest of the book enforces on every chapter."
msgstr ""
"大多数读者不会按顺序读到这一章。有的人会从搜索引擎落到这里，有的人从一场大会的演讲，有的人从同事在 Slack "
"里发来的一个链接。他们先需要的是一件事：一份 "
"**定义**——简明到可以被引用、辩护到可以被信赖、边界清晰到能与这个领域最常被混淆的另外五门学科区分开。本章在五小节里交付这份定义，之后是本书其余章节都要遵循的\"研究脉络\"和\"动手环节\"。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:19
#: 81fbd50c2f584970961d2180c91e3258
msgid "§03.1 A One-Sentence Definition"
msgstr "§03.1 一句话定义"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:21
#: 3ef754ad22da46ceb661e38402f8a790
msgid ""
"**Harness Engineering is the discipline of deliberately designing, "
"operating, and evolving the structures that surround an AI coding agent so "
"that the software it produces is verifiable, observable, and "
"understandable.**"
msgstr ""
"**Harness Engineering（驾驭工程）是这样一门学科：有意识地设计、运行并演进环绕在 AI "
"编码智能体周围的那些结构，以使它所产出的软件具备可验证、可观测、可理解这三项属性。**"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:25
#: aa5c36713f8e401da706ff4484d7beff
msgid ""
"Unpack that sentence once. *Deliberately designing* rejects the default "
"position — that whatever happens to be in the prompt window, the IDE, and "
"the CI pipeline constitutes an adequate environment for an AI agent. "
"*Operating and evolving* says a harness is not a one-time setup; entropy "
"creeps in across runs, and a harness that is not tended drifts into a "
"collection of stale instructions. *Verifiable, observable, and "
"understandable* names the three guardians Chapter 04 unpacks — the "
"properties the harness exists to guarantee. The agent is not the subject of "
"the sentence; the *structures around it* are. That inversion is the whole of"
" the field."
msgstr ""
"把这句话拆开读一遍。*有意识地设计*，拒绝了那种默认立场——认为不管提示词窗口里、IDE 里、CI "
"流水线里正好有什么，就已经是智能体的足够环境了。*运行并演进*，则是在说挽具不是一次性架起来就完事的东西；熵会在一次次运行之间悄悄爬进来，没人伺候的挽具会漂移成一堆过时的指令。*可验证、可观测、可理解*，点出了第"
" 04 章要展开的\"三大护法\"——挽具存在的目的就是为了保证这三项属性。句子的主语不是智能体；*围绕在它周围的那些结构* "
"才是。这一主语的翻转，就是这整门学科的全部。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:35
#: 8b815245eeb44fe0ae5905c062929eee
msgid "§03.2 Operational Boundary"
msgstr "§03.2 操作性边界"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:37
#: 2e076dafd83147f0b25dec2056540a84
msgid ""
"A harness is a concrete, enumerable set of engineering artefacts. The field "
"becomes tractable only when we say exactly what is in the set and what is "
"not."
msgstr "挽具是一组具体的、可以枚举出来的工程制品。只有当我们把这个集合里 *有什么* 和 *没有什么* 说清楚，这门学科才变得可操作。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:41
#: 352d3f73b31b430e8dfc3186aa73b38f
msgid "A harness IS"
msgstr "挽具 *是* 什么"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:43
#: 7917b3ae3af34ce0b000758f1878b06a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Prompts, skills, and agent-facing specs** — `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, "
"`SKILL.md`, MCP server manifests, and system prompts treated as versioned, "
"reviewable code {cite}`anthropic2024claudecode,anthropic2024mcp`."
msgstr ""
"**提示词、技能，以及面向智能体的规约**——`CLAUDE.md`、`AGENTS.md`、`SKILL.md`、MCP 服务器的 "
"manifest，以及那些被当作纳入版本控制、可审阅的代码来对待的系统提示词 "
"{cite}`anthropic2024claudecode,anthropic2024mcp`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:46
#: 805bab8a1c2444028643ccebfb21b8e1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Approval gates and fences** — pre-commit hooks, lint rules, PR reviewers, "
"required CI checks, and any automation that refuses a bad artefact "
"regardless of who (or what) authored it "
"{cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery`."
msgstr ""
"**审批关卡与护栏**——pre-commit 钩子、lint 规则、PR 评审人、必过的 CI "
"检查，以及任何不论作者是谁（或是什么）都会拒绝坏制品的自动化 {cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:49
#: 6c180af69b44444c9c89679fb22a9b4f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A sandbox** — container, VM, scoped filesystem, or ephemeral worktree "
"inside which the agent operates without touching production "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`."
msgstr ""
"**一个沙箱**——容器、VM、受限文件系统，或临时 worktree——让智能体在其中操作，而不去碰生产环境 "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:52
#: 7aa4e19da431442f8e80b9b0d9f78158
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Documentation addressed to the agent** — runbooks, architectural decision "
"records, and skill files the agent can read on its own to reduce ambient "
"hallucination {cite}`martraire2019living`."
msgstr ""
"**写给智能体看的文档**——运维手册（runbooks）、架构决策记录（ADR）、以及智能体能独自读取、用来减少环境性幻觉的技能文件 "
"{cite}`martraire2019living`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:55
#: c5c1714c084e4520b18d434828a6c2bc
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Metrics and a feedback surface** — observable signals (test pass rate, "
"cost per turn, lint violation count, time-to-green) written down somewhere "
"the team reviews weekly {cite}`majors2022observability`."
msgstr ""
"**度量与反馈面**——可观测的信号（测试通过率、每轮成本、lint 违规数、time-to-green）被写在一处、由团队每周复盘 "
"{cite}`majors2022observability`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:59
#: 5d2c4ba1b42e4ebfb7516c7beb17404d
msgid "A harness IS NOT"
msgstr "挽具 *不是* 什么"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:61
#: 7605c440665741dbbd83bb699776d2d0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A runtime inference stack.** How the model's tokens are scheduled on which"
" GPUs is infrastructure, not harness — that is the domain of *AI "
"Engineering* in Huyen's sense {cite}`huyen2025aieng`."
msgstr ""
"**运行时推理栈。** 模型的 token 被如何调度到哪些 GPU 上，是基础设施的事，不是挽具——那是 Huyen 意义上的 *AI "
"Engineering* 的领地 {cite}`huyen2025aieng`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:64
#: fec31b81a24f45da82836b4054843a3d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**An ML evaluation benchmark.** HELM, MMLU, Terminal-Bench and their "
"relatives measure an agent; they are *inputs* to harness design, not the "
"harness itself {cite}`langchain2026tbench`."
msgstr ""
"**ML 评测基准。** HELM、MMLU、Terminal-Bench 这一族度量的是智能体本身；它们是挽具设计的 *输入*，而不是挽具 "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:67
#: 62bf7b681aad40288c4171eff0cb0614
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**An IDE plugin surface.** Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf and their siblings are "
"*clients* that consume a harness; the harness lives in the repository and "
"outlives any specific editor {cite}`peng2023copilotstudy`."
msgstr ""
"**IDE 插件面。** Cursor、Copilot、Windsurf 等等是消费挽具的 *客户端*；挽具住在仓库里，比任何一个具体的编辑器活得都长 "
"{cite}`peng2023copilotstudy`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:70
#: c690c0b01f244d26a6c2e29ce82f88ed
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**An agent framework SDK.** LangChain, AutoGen, CrewAI, and LangGraph expose"
" building blocks for multi-step agents; the harness is what a team writes "
"*around* whatever framework it chooses {cite}`langchain2026tbench`."
msgstr ""
"**智能体框架 SDK。** LangChain、AutoGen、CrewAI、LangGraph 提供的是多步智能体的构件；挽具是团队在它所选框架 "
"*外围* 写出来的东西 {cite}`langchain2026tbench`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:73
#: a40b5e1c8d1346e983ed1ef61935db29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A deployment pipeline.** DevOps owns the path from merged commit to "
"production; harness ownership ends at the merged commit "
"{cite}`forsgren2018accelerate`."
msgstr ""
"**部署流水线。** 从已合并的 commit 到生产环境的那条路由 DevOps 负责；挽具的职责边界，到\"已合并的 commit\"为止 "
"{cite}`forsgren2018accelerate`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:77
#: 8437b21367e24f00911bb8c38067ddcf
msgid ""
"The membership test is simple: if the artefact shapes what the agent *tries "
"to produce* before a commit lands, it is harness; if it shapes what happens "
"*to* a commit afterwards, it is DevOps; if it shapes how the model itself is"
" served, it is AI Engineering."
msgstr ""
"归属判定很简单：一件制品塑造的是智能体在 commit 落地之前 *试图产出什么*，它就是挽具；它塑造的是 commit 之后 *这个 commit "
"会被怎么对待*，它就是 DevOps；它塑造的是模型本身如何被服务化，它就是 AI Engineering。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:82
#: 5cad88823ce447cdaed63072e5b53f30
msgid ""
"Three edge cases recur often enough to be worth walking explicitly; each is "
"a case where the membership test is easy to misapply."
msgstr "有三种边界情形出现得足够频繁，值得明确走一遍；在这些情形下，上面这条归属判定很容易被误用。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:85
#: 875e14a0a80f4d468d0ad048e71b0017
msgid ""
"**A flaky pre-commit hook**. Is it harness? Yes — it fires before commit — "
"but it is a *degraded* harness artefact because it has lost the property the"
" harness exists to supply. The fence that refuses intermittently teaches the"
" agent (and the humans) that the fence is optional. A flaky fence is worse "
"than no fence at all, because it combines the cost of the fence with none of"
" its leverage. Fix the flakiness or delete the hook; do not leave it half-"
"alive."
msgstr ""
"**一个 flaky 的 pre-commit 钩子。** 算不算挽具？算——它在 commit 之前触发——但它是一件 *退化* "
"的挽具制品，因为它丢掉了挽具存在所要提供的那份属性。一道时灵时不灵的护栏，教会智能体（和人）一件事：这道护栏是可选的。一道 flaky "
"的护栏比没有护栏还糟，因为它同时背上了护栏的成本，却交不出护栏的杠杆。修好它的不稳定性，要么就把这条钩子删掉；不要留它半死不活。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:92
#: 8213476ecec4440e84ad30ddf7a97e67
msgid ""
"**A dashboard that no one reads**. Is it harness? No — it fails the "
"*operated-and-evolved* half of the definition. Instrumentation without a "
"review cadence is observability infrastructure, not MDD. Chapter 06's Groom "
"column exists specifically to prevent this demotion."
msgstr ""
"**一块没人看的仪表盘。** 算不算挽具？不算——它在定义里 *\"运行并演进\"* "
"这半句上就过不了关。没有复盘节奏的埋点，属于可观测性基础设施，而不是 MDD。第 06 章的 *梳理（Groom）* "
"这一列，正是为了防止它落到这种退位状态。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:96
#: eb19baf08e784fb280028710810bef62
msgid ""
"**A long `README.md` pinned to the top of the repo**. Is it harness? Only if"
" the agent reads it on every turn. A `README.md` addressed primarily to "
"human newcomers is documentation; a `README.md` whose first fifty lines the "
"agent loads into its context window on session start (verify by inspecting "
"the agent's context dump) is harness. The file's filename does not determine"
" the class; the consumer does."
msgstr ""
"**一份挂在仓库顶部的长 `README.md`。** 算不算挽具？只有当智能体每一轮都读它，它才算。主要写给新来的人看的 `README.md` "
"是文档；而一份智能体在会话开始时把前五十行加载进上下文窗口的 "
"`README.md`（可以通过检查智能体的上下文转储来验证）才是挽具。文件的名字不决定它归哪一类，*消费者* 决定它归哪一类。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:103
#: 229e428c8a2b4cc7aaf42033dcfeccbd
msgid ""
"Apply the membership test to your own repo for five minutes. Most teams "
"discover that *some* of their harness is accidentally misclassified as "
"documentation, and *some* of their documentation is accidentally treated as "
"harness — with neither pool tended by the right discipline."
msgstr ""
"花五分钟，把这条归属判定用在你自己的仓库上。大多数团队都会发现：他们挽具里的 *某些* 东西被误归成了文档，而他们文档里的 *某些* "
"东西被当成挽具来用——而这两坨，都没有被该管它们的那门学科好好伺候着。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:108
#: 31d9ba7844d6443fbc64de249ead454b
