msgstr "提示词脆弱、工具调用幻觉、无界的智能体循环"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:139
#: c0b08429005c4cee8552e0cdaee9a8fb
msgid ""
"Harness Engineering is the *environment-side* counterpart; agent engineering"
" builds the agent, harness engineering builds what the agent operates inside"
msgstr ""
"Harness Engineering 是它 *环境侧* 的对偶；agent engineering 造智能体，harness engineering "
"造智能体在其中运转的那个场"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:142
#: 0c04276445e34b68887b5de61fd9abcd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Platform Engineering** {cite}`cncf2024platformeng`"
msgstr "**Platform Engineering（平台工程）** {cite}`cncf2024platformeng`"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:143
#: da0652291a5c4764808d063e6cf22962
msgid ""
"Self-service developer platforms (IDPs) that abstract infra for product "
"teams"
msgstr "为产品团队抽象出基础设施的自助开发者平台（IDP）"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:145
#: 39579af84d7d4085a5d6252da23f6672
msgid "Golden paths, platform APIs, internal dev portals"
msgstr "黄金路径、平台 API、内部开发者门户"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:146
#: 30168ba2e4fc441d8cd98c1ef87547d8
msgid ""
"Cognitive load on platform consumers; drift between platform and reality"
msgstr "平台使用者的认知负担；平台与现实之间的漂移"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:148
#: 5408987a73bf46a688607ec2dfc1b33b
msgid ""
"Shares the \"paved road\" ideology; a mature Harness Engineering team "
"eventually exposes its harness as an internal platform product"
msgstr ""
"共享\"铺好的路（paved road）\"这种理念；一个成熟的 Harness Engineering "
"团队，最终会把自己的挽具作为一款内部平台产品对外暴露"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:152
#: d99c057526e74c12a8af2e0178fb514f
msgid ""
"Reading the table row by row clarifies the field's position: Harness "
"Engineering sits **between** AI/Agent Engineering (which is about the agent)"
" and DevOps (which is about deployment), and borrows artefact patterns from "
"both while owning neither."
msgstr ""
"一行一行读这张表，能把这个领域的位置看清楚：Harness Engineering 坐在 AI／Agent Engineering（关心的是智能体）和 "
"DevOps（关心的是部署）**之间**，从两边都借来了制品的模式，却哪一边都不归它管。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:157
#: 02105b2bffb4401c8917d12d83d5db70
msgid "§03.4 A Minimal Example"
msgstr "§03.4 一个最小示例"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:159
#: 17862a9d0033473fb0ec660977935b10
msgid ""
"A harness does not require a platform team or a budget. It requires three "
"files, each under ten lines. The triad below is the smallest complete "
"harness this book will ask the reader to ship — one specification for the "
"agent to read, one fence the agent (and humans) cannot bypass, and one "
"observability receipt the team publishes."
msgstr ""
"搭一具挽具不需要平台团队，也不需要预算。它需要的是三份文件，每份不到十行。下面这组三件套就是本书要求读者交付的最小完整挽具——一份让智能体读的规约、一道智能体（和人）都绕不过去的护栏、一份由团队对外公开的可观测性回执。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:165
#: 3372e5954ace4a6d819c8ddde92ff875
msgid "Fragment 1 — The specification the agent reads (`CLAUDE.md`)"
msgstr "片段 1 —— 让智能体读的那份规约（`CLAUDE.md`）"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:167
#: 74d469f1fc5949bbb6f1058fc27b15e4
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · CLAUDE.md fragment · 10 lines -->\n"
"\n"
"# Project: todo-cli\n"
"\n"
"**Language:** Python 3.11 · **Entry point:** `todo/__main__.py` · **Tests:** `pytest`\n"
"\n"
"## House rules for the agent\n"
"\n"
"- Never edit `todo/storage.py` without first running `pytest tests/test_storage.py`.\n"
"- Every new subcommand gets (a) a `--help` string, (b) a `tests/test_<cmd>.py` fixture.\n"
"- Commits must pass `pre-commit run --all-files`; see `pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml`.\n"
"- Observability contract lives in `harnesscard.fragment.yaml`; update it when adding a guardian.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · CLAUDE.md fragment · 10 lines -->\n"
"\n"
"# Project: todo-cli\n"
"\n"
"**Language:** Python 3.11 · **Entry point:** `todo/__main__.py` · **Tests:** `pytest`\n"
"\n"
"## House rules for the agent\n"
"\n"
"- Never edit `todo/storage.py` without first running `pytest tests/test_storage.py`.\n"
"- Every new subcommand gets (a) a `--help` string, (b) a `tests/test_<cmd>.py` fixture.\n"
"- Commits must pass `pre-commit run --all-files`; see `pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml`.\n"
"- Observability contract lives in `harnesscard.fragment.yaml`; update it when adding a guardian.\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:171
#: 85659f5c05064b648da6e6e511081460
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Three choices matter here. The rules are *few* (four bullets), because "
"agents respect short, enumerable house rules more reliably than long essays "
"{cite}`anthropic2024claudecode`. Each rule is *machine-checkable* (it names "
"a file, a command, or a config), so the spec aligns with the gate. And it "
"*points at its sibling artefacts* (pre-commit config, HarnessCard), so the "
"agent reading it knows where to look next."
msgstr ""
"这里有三处选择很关键。规则 *少*（只有四条），因为比起长篇大论，智能体更可靠地尊重短的、可枚举的\"家规\" "
"{cite}`anthropic2024claudecode`。每条规则都是 *机器可核验* "
"的（它点名一个文件、一条命令、一份配置），于是规约和关卡能对得上。而它 *指向自己兄弟制品*（pre-commit "
"配置、HarnessCard），这样读它的智能体就知道下一站该去哪里。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:178
#: 52cd3b7091ce40b2aa7686c33394301c
msgid ""
"Fragment 2 — The fence humans and agents alike cannot bypass (`.pre-commit-"
"config.yaml`)"
msgstr "片段 2 —— 人和智能体都绕不过去的那道护栏（`.pre-commit-config.yaml`）"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:180
#: 3f372f0f774044379f5cb075909b89f0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · .pre-commit-config.yaml fragment · 10 lines\n"
"repos:\n"
"  - repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit\n"
"    rev: v0.6.9\n"
"    hooks: [{id: ruff, args: [--fix]}, {id: ruff-format}]\n"
"  - repo: local\n"
"    hooks:\n"
"      - id: pytest-fast\n"
"        name: pytest (fast lane)\n"
"        entry: pytest -q -m \"not slow\"\n"
"        language: system\n"
"        pass_filenames: false\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · .pre-commit-config.yaml fragment · 10 lines\n"
"repos:\n"
"  - repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit\n"
"    rev: v0.6.9\n"
"    hooks: [{id: ruff, args: [--fix]}, {id: ruff-format}]\n"
"  - repo: local\n"
"    hooks:\n"
"      - id: pytest-fast\n"
"        name: pytest (fast lane)\n"
"        entry: pytest -q -m \"not slow\"\n"
"        language: system\n"
"        pass_filenames: false\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:184
#: 1056b410029048f982489b13cbbe0ef0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Pre-commit is the smallest possible TDD-style gate: it refuses bad code "
"regardless of authorship {cite}`beck2002tdd`. The ruff hook enforces style "
"(which the agent would otherwise hallucinate in five competing flavours) and"
" a tiny `pytest -m \"not slow\"` hook ensures no commit lands without a "
"fast-lane green. This is the *verifiability guardian* of Chapter 04 "
"compressed into ten lines."
msgstr ""
"pre-commit 是一道尽可能最小的 TDD 式关卡：它拒绝坏代码，不管作者是谁 {cite}`beck2002tdd`。ruff "
"钩子强制代码风格（否则智能体会在五种互相打架的风格之间幻觉出一种），而一个小小的 `pytest -m \"not slow\"` 钩子保证：没有一个 "
"commit 可以在快通道还没跑绿的情况下落地。这就是第 04 章那条 *可验证性护法* 被压缩进十行里的样子。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:191
#: e0d8670bb1854001864898550f0c79f3
msgid "Fragment 3 — The observability receipt (`harnesscard.yaml`)"
msgstr "片段 3 —— 可观测性回执（`harnesscard.yaml`）"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:193
#: 1ed16994e80e4398a739ca5489b02ca0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · HarnessCard fragment · 10 lines\n"
"harnesscard_version: \"0.2\"\n"
"project: todo-cli\n"
"sdd:   {spec: CLAUDE.md, owner: walter, last_reviewed: 2026-04-17}\n"
"tdd:   {gate: pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml, coverage_floor: 0.80}\n"
"mdd:   {signals: [pytest_pass_rate, ruff_violations, mean_agent_turns_to_green]}\n"
"approval_gate: pre-commit\n"
"evolution_log: CHANGELOG.md\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · HarnessCard fragment · 10 lines\n"
"harnesscard_version: \"0.2\"\n"
"project: todo-cli\n"
"sdd:   {spec: CLAUDE.md, owner: walter, last_reviewed: 2026-04-17}\n"
"tdd:   {gate: pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml, coverage_floor: 0.80}\n"
"mdd:   {signals: [pytest_pass_rate, ruff_violations, mean_agent_turns_to_green]}\n"
"approval_gate: pre-commit\n"
"evolution_log: CHANGELOG.md\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:197
#: 64d00ec2b4434cd09c4c0ae06aa59eb8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The HarnessCard is a standardised disclosure format proposed by the CAR "
"decomposition paper {cite}`car2025decomposition`. It names — in one commit-"
"reviewable file — which spec the harness uses, which gate enforces it, and "
"which signals the team watches. It is the smallest possible MDD surface "
"(Chapter 04's third guardian): three lines of signals is enough to start a "
"weekly review habit."
msgstr ""
"HarnessCard 是由 CAR 分解那篇论文提出的一种标准化披露格式 {cite}`car2025decomposition`。它在 *一份可作为"
" commit 被审阅的文件* 里点明：这具挽具用的是哪份规约、由哪道关卡强制执行、团队在看哪几路信号。它是一个尽可能最小的 MDD 面（第 04 "
"章那第三条护法）：三行信号，已经足够起一个每周复盘的习惯。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:204
#: 4d6bb7f4d5524b7e9a48c2dd6429d78b
msgid ""
"Taken together, these thirty lines satisfy the one-sentence definition "
"above. They are *deliberately designed* (not accidentally accumulated), "
"*operated and evolved* (the HarnessCard dates itself), and they explicitly "
"name the three guardians. Any team with an agent in the loop can ship this "
"triad in an afternoon and have a harness — primitive, but real."
msgstr ""
"把这三份加在一起的这三十行，已经满足了上面那句一句话的定义。它们是 *有意识设计* 的（不是偶然堆起来的）、是 *被运行和演进* "
"的（HarnessCard "
"自己就带着日期），并且明明白白点出了三大护法。任何一支有智能体参与的团队，都可以在一个下午把这一组三件套落地出来——它是一具挽具，虽然初级，但真实。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:211
#: 9bee714a1a0c4045b1d5aec33a6e1e36
msgid "Pitfall — The three files that look like a harness but are not"
msgstr "陷阱——长得像挽具、其实不是挽具的三份文件"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:214
#: 070fdf1cd0854cd4ae768107822972d1
msgid ""
"It is deceptively easy to produce a thirty-line triad that *looks* like the "
"one above but fails the membership test. Three common degenerate forms:"
msgstr "一组 *看起来* 和上面那一组一模一样、却过不了归属判定的三十行三件套，其实容易得惊人。常见的退化形态有三种："

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:218
#: c08adf71a686432e82cf54bcadc46469
msgid ""
"**The aspirational `CLAUDE.md`.** Rules written as wishes — \"write "
"idiomatic Go\", \"prefer clear names\" — that no hook can mechanically "
"falsify. The agent signals compliance and hallucinates adherence. **Test**: "
"every rule must name a file, a command, or a config. If none do, it is a "
"wish list."
msgstr ""
"**愿望型的 `CLAUDE.md`。** 规则被写成愿望——\"写地道的 "
"Go\"、\"倾向于清晰的命名\"——没有任何钩子能机械地证伪这些话。智能体于是打出合规的信号、幻觉出自己在遵守。**判定**：每一条规则都必须点名一个文件、一条命令、一份配置。若一条都没有，这就是一份愿望清单，不是规约。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:223
#: 7dfcebbada064bfa840babf449b212fe
msgid ""
"**The passing pre-commit.** A hook that runs `pytest` against a suite of "
"zero tests, or `ruff` against files in an excluded directory. It always "
"passes; the team loses the fence without ever noticing. **Test**: on first "
"install, the hook must *refuse* some artefact the repository currently "
"contains (even if you then fix that artefact). A fence that has never said "
"*no* is not a fence."
msgstr ""
"**永远能过的 pre-commit。** 一条钩子，拿 `pytest` 去跑一个测试数为零的套件，或者拿 `ruff` "
"去扫一个被排除掉的目录。它永远通过，而团队根本注意不到自己已经失去了这道护栏。**判定**：首次装上去时，这条钩子必须 *拒绝* "
"仓库里当前存在的某件制品（哪怕你接着就修掉了它）。从没说过一个 *不* 字的护栏，根本不是护栏。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:229
#: c1e1b9fee3994733b7924063b5182931
msgid ""
"**The undated HarnessCard.** A yaml file committed once and never touched. "
"The signals remain listed; none of them have moved in a quarter. **Test**: "
"the HarnessCard must carry a `last_reviewed:` date no more than thirty days "
"old, and the review must produce a delta note. A static HarnessCard is "
"ornament."
msgstr ""
"**没有日期的 HarnessCard。** 一份 "
"yaml，提交过一次之后就再也没人动过。信号列表还在，但整整一个季度，没有一路信号变过。**判定**：HarnessCard 必须带一个 "
"`last_reviewed:` 日期，且这个日期不超过三十天；而每一次复盘都必须产出一条 delta 笔记。一份静态的 HarnessCard "
"是装饰品。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:235
#: 00c6f85af7dd4664b46f339c901e1fe1
msgid ""
"The distinction between a working harness and harness theatre is not file "
"count — it is whether *on any given Tuesday* each of the three files can be "
"shown to have refused, measured, or steered something. If the answer is no "
"for a whole quarter, the triad has decayed into decoration even if its "
"contents are unchanged."
msgstr ""
"一具在工作的挽具和\"挽具剧场\"之间的分界，不在文件数——而在 "
"*随便挑一个周二*，这三份文件中的每一份，能不能拿得出\"它在最近拒绝过、量过、或引导过什么\"的证据。如果一整个季度的答案都是\"不能\"，那即便它的内容一字未改，这组三件套也已经衰退成装饰了。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:242
#: 3bf1c5c9b1854bb297f02ae1a99af858
msgid "§03.5 When Not to Use Harness Engineering"
msgstr "§03.5 什么时候 *不* 用 Harness Engineering"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:244
#: 4a053168aad44a828e5f269f3b77639e
msgid ""
"Harness Engineering, like any discipline, has a cost: three files to "
"maintain, a weekly review cadence, a HarnessCard to update. Three situations"
" do not pay that cost back:"
msgstr ""
"Harness Engineering 和任何一门学科一样，都是有成本的：三份文件要维护、一个每周复盘的节奏、一张 HarnessCard "
"要更新。有三种情形，这份成本收不回来："

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:248
#: f9d428c7e2b641e7b29cee02b1097ed5
msgid ""
"**One-off throwaway scripts.** A 40-line script that parses a CSV and exits "
"is not a project; it has no second commit. The harness investment does not "
"amortise over a second commit that never arrives."
msgstr ""
"**一次性的一次就扔的脚本。** 一段 40 行、解析完 CSV 就退出的脚本不是一个项目；它没有第二次 "
"commit。挽具的那份投入，摊不到一个永远不会到来的\"第二次 commit\"上。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:251
#: 328ec298d7da479ebc1ea39824491ad5
msgid ""
"**Solo prototypes with zero AI usage.** If a developer neither uses nor "
"plans to use an AI coding agent, Chapters 04–06 still apply as traditional "
"SE hygiene, but the *harness* label is unhelpful — the \"agent\" whose "
"environment is being shaped does not exist."
msgstr ""
"**完全不用 AI 的个人原型。** 如果一个开发者既没有、也不打算使用 AI 编码智能体，第 04–06 章依然可以作为传统软件工程卫生学来读，但 "
"*挽具* 这个标签在这里不帮任何忙——那个被\"塑造环境\"的\"智能体\"根本不存在。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:255
#: a30973ee1f9d4d03b6268cf4cfb597fb
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Legacy code no AI agent will ever touch.** A 2008 COBOL system under "
"change freeze gains nothing from a `CLAUDE.md`; effort is better spent on "
"Feathers' legacy-code playbook {cite}`feathers2004legacy` until the code "
"base re-enters active development with AI in the loop."
msgstr ""
"**任何 AI 智能体都不会碰的遗留代码。** 一个 2008 年的 COBOL 系统，已经处在变更冻结下，给它加一份 `CLAUDE.md` "
"毫无收益；把精力花在 Feathers 的那套遗留代码手册上更值得 {cite}`feathers2004legacy`，直到哪天这套代码库带着 AI "
"重新进入活跃开发。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:260
#: 8ed65812461742c68cd61b65eac3ec3b
msgid ""
"Anywhere else — from a solo side project with Copilot autocomplete to a "
"fifty-engineer platform team running autonomous agents — the cost of the "
"thirty-line triad in §03.4 is lower than the cost of its absence."
msgstr ""
"除此以外的所有情形——从一位独自搞副业、只用 Copilot 做自动补全的开发者，到五十个人跑着自主智能体的平台团队——§03.4 "
"那三十行三件套的成本，都低于没有它的成本。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:264
#: c0afa407a5a546cd90bdc053fb17682a
msgid "Research Foundations"
msgstr "研究脉络"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:266
#: e2b0b9bc6e034cc3969213f678f5abb9
msgid ""
"The definition of Harness Engineering in §03.1 is deliberately constructed "
"to sit between established disciplines rather than to invent a new one; its "
"credibility therefore rests on the boundary citations rather than on a "
"single primary source."
msgstr ""
"§03.1 里 Harness Engineering 的定义是 *有意* "
"构造得坐在几门已有学科之间，而不是另起炉灶；因此它的可信度靠的是一串边界引用，而不是哪一个\"唯一源头\"。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:271
#: aaa0d71bfb7d40bd92519d36b9b72c66
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**DevOps baseline:** Humble & Farley's *Continuous Delivery* "
"{cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery` and Forsgren, Humble & Kim's "
"*Accelerate* {cite}`forsgren2018accelerate` establish that an approval-gate "
"discipline can be culturally normalised across an entire industry; the "
"harness borrows their gate-centric stance wholesale while redirecting it "
"upstream of the commit rather than downstream."
msgstr ""
"**DevOps 基线。** Humble 与 Farley 的 *Continuous Delivery* "
"{cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery`、Forsgren／Humble／Kim 的 *Accelerate* "
"{cite}`forsgren2018accelerate`，合起来建立了一件事：一套\"审批关卡\"纪律可以在整个行业里被文化化地标准化。挽具几乎是原样借走了他们这种以关卡为中心的立场，只是把它从"
" commit 的 *下游* 重新指向了 *上游*。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:277
#: 4ccb9b06438f4757946a8f8042f46f20
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**MLOps baseline:** Sculley et al.'s *Hidden Technical Debt in Machine "
"Learning Systems* {cite}`sculley2015mltechdebt` is the canonical warning "
"about invisible glue code in ML pipelines; Huyen's *AI Engineering* "
"{cite}`huyen2025aieng` updates that critique for the foundation-model era "
"and is the reference behind the \"AI is not harness\" row in §03.3."
msgstr ""
"**MLOps 基线。** Sculley 等人 *Hidden Technical Debt in Machine Learning Systems*"
" {cite}`sculley2015mltechdebt`，是关于 ML 流水线里那些隐形粘合代码的经典警示；Huyen 的 *AI "
"Engineering* {cite}`huyen2025aieng` 则把那份批评在\"基础模型时代\"里做了更新，也就是 §03.3 里\"AI "
"不等于挽具\"这一行背后真正的参考。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:282
#: fa8cf6f3e52245b2aab82287c8fe515e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Agent Engineering boundary:** Anthropic's *Building Effective Agents* "
"{cite}`anthropic2024agents` and LangChain's *Terminal-Bench 2.0* "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench` are the two most-cited 2024–2026 sources on what"
" an agent is and how to evaluate one; both frame the agent as the subject "
"and the environment as an implementation detail, which is the precise "
"framing this book inverts."
msgstr ""
"**Agent Engineering 边界。** Anthropic 的 *Building Effective Agents* "
"{cite}`anthropic2024agents` 与 LangChain 的 *Terminal-Bench 2.0* "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench`，是 2024–2026 "
"年间关于\"智能体是什么、该如何评估它\"这个问题最常被引用的两份资料；两份都把智能体当成主语，把环境当成实现细节——而本书要翻转的，恰恰就是这个主语／宾语关系。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:288
#: 81a39238676c4adfb081bbb12c0a18db
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Platform Engineering boundary:** the CNCF Platforms Working Group's "
"*Platform Engineering Maturity Model* {cite}`cncf2024platformeng` anchors "
"the \"paved road\" vocabulary §03.3 borrows in its Platform Engineering row."
msgstr ""
"**Platform Engineering 边界。** CNCF Platforms Working Group 的 *Platform "
"Engineering Maturity Model* {cite}`cncf2024platformeng`，正是 §03.3 里 Platform "
"Engineering 那一行所借用的\"铺好的路（paved road）\"词汇背后的锚点。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:292
#: 92dcbdd20dd543c3ae7ee550d6c741ff
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Harness-Engineering primary sources:** the CAR decomposition and "
"HarnessCard from the position paper {cite}`car2025decomposition`, Fowler's "
"bliki entry that first named the practice {cite}`fowler2026harness`, "
"OpenAI's vendor-side articulation {cite}`openai2026harness`, and "
"Thoughtworks' Technology Radar trial-ring entry "
"{cite}`thoughtworks2026harness` together constitute the four primary-source "
"references this book cross-cites when the label \"Harness Engineering\" "
"itself is at stake."
msgstr ""
"**Harness Engineering 第一手来源。** 立场论文中提出的 CAR 分解与 HarnessCard "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`、Fowler 首次为这项实践命名的 bliki 条目 "
"{cite}`fowler2026harness`、OpenAI 在厂商一侧的表述 {cite}`openai2026harness`，以及 "
"Thoughtworks 技术雷达中 trial 环的那条条目 {cite}`thoughtworks2026harness`——每当\"Harness"
" Engineering\"这个名字本身需要被交叉引用时，本书用的就是这四份第一手参考。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:301
#: 7f071e5b77394905a7703100bcced93e
msgid "Hands-On"
msgstr "动手环节"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:303
#: 0c4d8da6b22842c19af53d434ffd3fa0
msgid ""
"The minimal example in §03.4 ships as three fragments under "
"`book/source/_handson/03-what-is-harness-engineering/`:"
msgstr ""
"§03.4 里那个最小示例，以三个片段的形式收在 `book/source/_handson/03-what-is-harness-"
"engineering/` 目录下："

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:306
#: 5f197c0a29f5455a97a65196a2191987
msgid "`claude-md.fragment.md` — the ten-line specification the agent reads."
msgstr "`claude-md.fragment.md`——给智能体读的那份十行规约。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:307
#: 236fec68539d42e98f4157e31b996ed4
msgid ""
"`pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml` — the ten-line fence that refuses bad "
"commits."
msgstr "`pre-commit-config.fragment.yaml`——那条拒绝坏 commit 的十行护栏。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:309
#: 41e84e0c7347407681fc491441b757a8
msgid ""
"`harnesscard.fragment.yaml` — the ten-line observability receipt the team "
"publishes."
msgstr "`harnesscard.fragment.yaml`——团队对外发布的那份十行可观测性回执。"

#: ../../source/chapters/03-what-is-harness-engineering.md:312
#: bc824c44d3f04c618397cf4b553d75d4
msgid ""
"The accompanying `README.md` names the reading order and the intent of each "
"file. A reader who only wants to *start* practising Harness Engineering "
"today can copy these three fragments into any repo, adjust the file names, "
"and begin the weekly HarnessCard review loop Chapter 06 formalises."
msgstr ""
"配套的 `README.md` 给出了阅读顺序，以及每一份文件的意图。如果一位读者今天就只想 *开始* 实践 Harness "
"Engineering，他把这三个片段拷进任何一个仓库，把文件名改一下，就可以启动第 06 章要正式化的那套 HarnessCard 每周复盘循环。"

